summary:
Files only: no API, no submit.
PUBLIC READ. The +0.002 from cap 6 (probe 45 exp70g 0.956, #268 -> #162) is about one net true division event on the public embryo.
PRIVATE VIEW (model). About 105-170 extra private insertions, ~5 of them scorable (2-10). One private TP is worth ~+0.0009, one FP ~-0.0003. The marginal precision is either public-like (~0.43) or lab-like (~0.18; the lab went 0 TP / 4 FP even in-sample), against a break-even of ~0.17-0.29. So C = exp70g - #37 on private is ~+0.0004 +- 0.002, with P(C > 0) ~0.5 (0.32-0.59): a coin flip whose spread is wider than the insertion itself.
FINALS TABLE. Round-16 MC re-based on the 19:43Z LB: bronze ~#400, silver ~#200, X (exact x138) private rank ~540. P(bronze+)/P(silver+) for the base mix, with the range over 10 scenarios:
- {#37,#38}: .53/.12 [.34-.85 / .04-.41];
- {exp70b,#38}: .54/.16 [.38-.84 / .07-.44];
- {exp70g,#37}: .67/.38 [.51-.84 / .20-.60];
- {exp70g,#38}: .52/.35 [.34-.75 / .16-.48];
- {exp70g,exp70b}: .69/.40 [.54-.85 / .23-.62];
- two cap files: .57/.42 (dominated).
RECOMMENDATION for the user's 29 Sep pick: {best cap-family file, its no-cap parent}, i.e. {exp70g, #37} now, or {exp70g, exp70b} as an equal alternative.
- {exp70g,#37} beats the ticked {#37,#38} in every scenario (+0.06..+0.21 bronze, +0.08..+0.33 silver), including the fully lab-adverse one.
- With a stalled field it ties on bronze and still wins silver.
- Never {cap, #38}; never two cap files.
- A higher-dose file (cap 8/12, thr 0.3) displaces exp70g only on a strictly higher display. Its partner is its nested parent: #37 for K2-based files, exp70b for fm45-based ones.
OTHER. No public observable flips the pick. An OOF cap lab is feasible on CPU but has no decision value. Nothing new reaches R8, and no new build is proposed.
